摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness plugin for Agentic Control Plane: logs and checks tool calls. Ask works; deny is reported, not enforced yet.","id":"gh:1333443629","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-acp-plugin","slug":"agentic-control-plane/dsh-acp-plugin","topics":["agent-security","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness plugin for Agentic Control Plane: logs and checks tool calls. Ask works; deny is re"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ported, not enforced yet."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# @agenticcontrolplane/dsh"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Agentic Control Plane for DeepSeek Harness: every tool call is checked and logged against your polic"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"ies, recording what ran, what was held, and why. Ask works. Deny is reported to the agent but not ye"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"t enforced (see the note below)."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> **Deny is not enforced yet.** When a policy says `deny`, the plugin reports it to the agent with t"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"he reason, but it does not stop the call today (the fix is tracked). Until that ships, treat dsh as "},{"id":"p4s3","text":"audit plus ask. See the coverage matrix."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> **Which ACP?** dsh also ships `packages/acp` in core. That one is Zed's Agent Client Protocol, the"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" editor↔agent standard, published as `@deepseek-ai/dsh-acp`. It is an unrelated project with the sam"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"e acronym. If you're wiring dsh into Zed or the AI SDK, you want that one; this plugin checks each t"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"ool call against your policies. The full map: agenticcontrolplane.com/acp-vs-acp."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Every decision also lands in your console with tool, decision, reason and latency. dsh's own Traject"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ory log and your ACP activity log are two independent records of the same history. One workspace cov"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"ers every harness you run, so the same rules apply to dsh, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and OpenClaw ("},{"id":"p7s4","text":"deny excepted, see the note above). Free for individuals."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"This is a native Cordis plugin on dsh's typed interception points, not a shell-hook shim. It registe"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"s a native Cordis plugin on dsh's typed interception points, not a shell-hook shim. It registers on:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- `tools/pre-execute`: the policy decision. `allow` lets the call through. `deny` is reported to the"},{"id":"p9s2","text":" agent with the reason, but the plugin does not stop the call yet. `ask` hands off to dsh's own appr"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"oval flow.\n- `tools/post-execute`: output scanning. A server-side block turns the result into correc"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"tive feedback; shadow-mode notices surface what enforcement *would* have done."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"> dsh itself requires **Node 22** (`Promise.withResolvers`, zstd streams). Under Node 20 the harness"},{"id":"p11s2","text":" fails at boot with errors that don't say so. Run `fnm install 22` first."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"That detects dsh, installs this plugin into every profile you have, opens your\nbrowser once to sign "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"in, and saves the key to `~/.acp/credentials`, which the\nplugin reads on its own. There is no token "},{"id":"p13s3","text":"to copy and nothing to export."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Manual install"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Credentials come from `~/.acp/credentials` (written by the installer above) or\nfrom `ACP_BEARER_TOKE"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"N` if you would rather set it yourself, which is useful on a\nheadless box. Get a key at\ncloud.agenti"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"ther set it yourself, which is useful on a\nheadless box. Get a key at\ncloud.agenticcontrolplane.com."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Confirm the row actually mounted. Installing the package and composing it into\nthe profile are two d"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"actually mounted. Installing the package and composing it into\nthe profile are two different things:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"If it isn't there, add `@agenticcontrolplane/dsh` to that profile's `package.json`\n`\"dsh.profile.bun"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"there, add `@agenticcontrolplane/dsh` to that profile's `package.json`\n`\"dsh.profile.bundles\"` list."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"No build step, no dependencies, plain ESM. Installing from git works too (`dsh plugin add github:age"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ntic-control-plane/dsh-acp-plugin`) and needs no build allowance."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"No key: the plugin prints a warning and lets the session run."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Override the row in your profile's `cordis.patch.yml`:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"`ACP_GOVERN_BASE`, `ACP_BEARER_TOKEN`, `ACP_AGENT_TIER`, and `ACP_SHADOW=off` work as environment va"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"BASE`, `ACP_BEARER_TOKEN`, `ACP_AGENT_TIER`, and `ACP_SHADOW=off` work as environment variables too."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## What happens if the gateway is down"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"If the gateway is down, dsh keeps working, and you are told the calls weren't checked:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- **Interactive sessions fail open, loudly.** If the gateway is unreachable, the call proceeds, a `["},{"id":"p28s2","text":"ACP] ⚠ UNGOVERNED` warning is logged, and a line lands in `~/.acp/lapse.log`.\n- **Unattended agents "},{"id":"p28s3","text":"fail closed.** With nobody watching, a call that can't be checked is blocked.\n- This posture only co"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"vers the inability to *ask* the policy. It does not change how a `deny` is handled (see the note at "},{"id":"p28s5","text":"inability to *ask* the policy. It does not change how a `deny` is handled (see the note at the top)."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"In headless compositions with no approval service mounted, dsh itself resolves `ask` to deny, so una"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"ttended runs cannot self-approve."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## Notes"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- Already running our Claude Code hook? dsh's `@deepseek-ai/dsh-hooks-claude-code` bridge runs an un"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"modified `hooks.json`, so `govern.mjs` works today with zero new code. Input rewriting is not suppor"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"ted on that path. This native plugin is the recommended path.\n- This package launched as `dsh-plugin"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"-acp`; that name still installs but is deprecated. Same code, so swap the name in your profile when "},{"id":"p31s5","text":"convenient. (The `cordis.patch.yml` in this repo still carries the old name.)"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Learn more"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"- What ACP can see and control in dsh: the controls reference\n- The launch write-up: dsh's intercept"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"ion surface, what the integration caught on day one, and where dsh lands on the cross-harness covera"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"ace, what the integration caught on day one, and where dsh lands on the cross-harness coverage table"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Test"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
